  "verbalization": "Hippurin-1 is implicated in the biological activity of SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Hippurin-1 acts as a target for VMRC-LCP and Phorone, which in turn target SMMC-7721. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Hippurin-1 serves as a starting point, leading to the activation of VMRC-LCP and Phorone, which ultimately affect SMMC-7721. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway highlights a potential mechanism by which Hippurin-1 influences SMMC-7721, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The integration of these targets suggests that Hippurin-1 may play a role in modulating the activity of these compounds, which could have implications for therapeutic applications. The evidence supports a mechanism where Hippurin-1 is involved in the regulation of SMMC-7721 through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
